# Addresses a reader can derive from this site's own pattern and not find.
#
# Parsed by Cloudflare Workers, never served as an asset — the file itself returns 404, which
# is why it does not appear in the sitemap and does not need a robots rule. Format is
# `from to status`, one per line, and 302 is the default status, so every line here says 301
# out loud: these are permanent facts about how this site is laid out, not a temporary move,
# and a 302 would have crawlers re-ask forever.
#
# WHY THESE AND NOT MORE. A redirect is a promise that an address means something, so each one
# has to be derivable rather than guessed. Two families qualify:
#
# 1. THE GAP IN THE PATTERN. Fifteen languages live in a directory named after them and the
#    sixteenth, English, lives at the root. A reader who has seen /uk/ and /de/ will type /en/,
#    and it is the one address the site's own layout invites and does not answer.
#
# 2. THE COUNTRY CODE FOR THE LANGUAGE CODE. The directories are ISO 639-1 language codes. The
#    two-letter code most people actually know is the country: cz, jp, kr, cn, br, ua. Each of
#    these differs from its language code, and each has exactly one language on this site it
#    could mean.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. /tw/ and /hk/ are not redirected to /zh/: this site's Chinese is
# zh_CN, simplified, and sending a Taiwanese or Hong Kong reader to it is a wrong answer with a
# political edge on it, not a near miss. And nothing is done about /uk/ meaning Ukrainian here
# while meaning Britain to most of the people who will type it — `uk` is the language code for
# Ukrainian and the page it serves is correct. A redirect cannot fix an ambiguity; it can only
# pick a side, and the side already picked is the one that is right.
#
# Every target below exists as a real page, and no source below shadows one:
# `redteam/test_readme.py` refuses this file otherwise. A redirect pointing at a 404 is two
# requests to arrive at the same nothing, and a redirect standing in front of a live page is
# how a page disappears without anybody deleting it.

/en/  /       301
/en   /       301

/ua/  /uk/    301
/ua   /uk/    301
/cz/  /cs/    301
/cz   /cs/    301
/jp/  /ja/    301
/jp   /ja/    301
/kr/  /ko/    301
/kr   /ko/    301
/cn/  /zh/    301
/cn   /zh/    301
/br/  /pt/    301
/br   /pt/    301
